## Static Checks To Run

Before packaging or claiming "ready", use the task-scoped static checker for repo-local structural/compliance checks only. It does not replace `collapse_check.py`, Harbor quality check, or agent-trial review:

```bash
python3 run_static_checks.py --task-dir tasks/<task-name> --version edition_2
```

This checker objectively enforces the current public-contract rules for declared user-visible outputs, literal `internal_harness_files` leakage in `instruction.md`, and milestone signal-completion directives.

Do NOT run bare `ci_checks/*.sh` scripts without a task path — they scan all `tasks/` by default, and legacy tasks will cause spurious failures.

If `ruff` is available: `ruff check tasks/<task-name>`.

## Packaging Verification

```bash
cd tasks/<task-name>
zip -rq ../../Task_Ready_To_Submit/<task-name>.zip . -x '*/__pycache__/*' '*.pyc' '.*'
python3 ../../validate_submission_zip.py ../../Task_Ready_To_Submit/<task-name>.zip
```

Verify: `instruction.md`, `task.toml`, `output_contract.toml`, `environment/`, `solution/`, and `tests/` at archive root. Append `--json` for machine-readable output.

## Single Approval Gate

Before claiming a hard task is approved or ready, first save a verifier-health report, then run the repo's single approval gate with the exact task directory, submission zip, Harbor job directory, and verifier-health JSON:

```bash
python3 verifier_health.py --task-dir tasks/<task-name> --output-json /tmp/<task-name>-verifier-health.json
python3 approve_task.py --task-dir tasks/<task-name> --zip Task_Ready_To_Submit/<task-name>.zip --job-dir jobs/<job-dir> --verifier-health /tmp/<task-name>-verifier-health.json
```

`approve_task.py` is the authoritative repo-local hard-task approval gate. It consumes the saved `verifier_health.py` report and bundles `run_static_checks.py`, `collapse_check.py`, `validate_submission_zip.py`, `analyze_trials.py`, manifest verification, and zip/source parity checks. Exit 0 is required before any `APPROVE`, `APPROVE WITH NOTE`, or "ready" claim on the default hard-only Edition 2 path.

